Subject: [PATCH 00/12] sunxi: bring up the PinePhone's MIPI-DSI panel

This series brings up the MIPI-DSI panel of the PinePhone in U-Boot and
makes the boot menu usable on the phone itself: the menu is drawn on the
panel, sized for it, and driven with the phone's three buttons. The
practical target is a UEFI boot loader menu (systemd-boot) readable and
usable without a serial adapter.

Patches 1-8 bring up the display. The sun6i MIPI-DSI host and its D-PHY
are ported from Linux (sun6i_mipi_dsi.c and phy-sun6i-mipi-dphy.c),
TCON0 learns the 8080/CPU mode the DSI host feeds from, and a driver is
added for the Xingbangda XBD599, the ST7703-class panel of the PinePhone
1.2. The pipeline is torn down again before the OS takes over, since the
kernel's driver fails to attach the panel when it finds the DSI block
streaming. Supporting fixes power the PMIC's GPIO LDOs that feed the
panel, honour num-interpolated-steps in pwm_backlight, and add the
A64's s_pwm pinmux function for the backlight PWM. A new
SUNXI_VIDCONSOLE_FIRST option lets a board put the panel at the head of
stdout, because EFI takes its console geometry from the first entry and
a menu drawn for 80x25 overflows a 45-column phone panel.

Patches 9-12 make the buttons a keyboard. A driver for the Allwinner
LRADC reads the volume keys (based on a Tow-Boot patch by Samuel
Dionne-Riel, itself based on work by Ondrej Jirman), and a new driver
reads the power key an AXP803 PMIC latches in its interrupt status.
The PinePhone maps them to up, down and enter through u-boot,code
properties in a U-Boot-only overlay, so the keys keep their meaning
under Linux.

The two halves are independent: the display stack (1-8) and the button
stack (9-12) each stand alone.

Tested on a PinePhone 1.2: U-Boot's console and the systemd-boot menu
render on the panel, the buttons drive the menu, and Linux 6.x attaches
the panel and brings the display up normally after handoff.

BeatLink (11):
  pinctrl: sunxi: add the A64's s_pwm function
  power: regulator: axp: support the GPIO pins used as LDOs
  video: pwm_backlight: honour num-interpolated-steps
  video: sunxi: add a sun6i MIPI-DSI host driver
  video: sunxi: drive TCON0 in DSI mode on the A64
  video: panel: add the Xingbangda XBD599
  sunxi: let a board put the panel at the head of stdout
  sunxi: pinephone: enable the display
  button: add a driver for the power key of an AXP PMIC
  sunxi: let button keyboards join stdin
  sunxi: pinephone: let the buttons drive the boot menu

Samuel Dionne-Riel (1):
  button: add a driver for the Allwinner LRADC

